<h2 class="wp-block-heading">In the Community</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong><a href="https://macsparky.circle.so/c/labs-discussion-board/stream-deck-button-icons">Stream Deck Button Icons</a></strong> (Labs Discussion Board)</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Good timing on this one. A member with two Stream Decks and 23 profiles got tired of hand-building SF Symbols icons, so he started generating them with ChatGPT and eventually built a custom GPT seeded with his ten best icons so everything new comes out in the same bronze-and-black style. The thread turned into a show-and-tell with screenshots of redesigned decks. The useful detail buried in the replies: a custom GPT holds the style tighter than a Project does, and it&#8217;s worth asking for bigger, higher-contrast text so the buttons stay readable at a glance.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong><a href="https://macsparky.circle.so/c/labs-discussion-board/lab-browser-discussion">Lab Browser Discussion</a></strong> (Labs Discussion Board)</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The browser conversation from the August meetup picked itself back up here. One member wrote out the four browsers he keeps open all the time and why each one gets its own job, and the first reply added DuckDuckGo and DEVONagent Pro to the pile. This is the raw material for the September jam session, so add yours now.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong><a href="https://macsparky.circle.so/c/labs-discussion-board/golden-gate-beta-experiences">Golden Gate beta experiences</a></strong> (Labs Discussion Board)</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">A member running the developer beta across three Macs had one thing break. Colorbyte&#8217;s ImagePrint stopped seeing an Epson P900, and the vendor confirmed it as a driver conflict. He came back this week with the fix. Manually installing Rosetta 2 got it working on beta 5.</p>



